<title>SRI LANKA: Weather - Showers seen over S.Lanka's north, west.</title>
<headline>Weather - Showers seen over S.Lanka's north, west.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's metereological department released the following rainfall figures for 24 hours ending Tuesday morning.</p>
<p>Hydro catchment areas (in mm):</p>
<p>    Bowathenna		0</p>
<p>    Canyon		    0.5</p>
<p>    Castlereigh	     0</p>
<p>    Kotmale		   0</p>
<p>    Laxapana		 32.0</p>
<p>    Moussakele		0</p>
<p>    Norton		    2.4</p>
<p>    Randenigala	     0</p>
<p>    Victoria		  0</p>
<p>    Samanalawewa	    0</p>
<p>    Ukuwela		   0</p>
<p>    Rantembe		  0</p>
<p>The department forecasts isolated showers over western and southern provinces on Wednesday. Showers are also likely to develop in the Central, Uva, Sabaragamuwa provinces during and afternoon and evening, the department said.</p>
</text>
